{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-011", "score": 0.137, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-011 | Study family SF-APPS-011: Regular season vs playoff PPP by play type (DRIVE over-prediction)\n- observed_research_question: Regular season vs playoff PPP by play type (DRIVE over-prediction)\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: DRIVE PPP is materially higher in RS than playoffs, so an RS-calibrated optimizer over-recommends DRIVE.\n- observed_result: DRIVE RS 1.198 vs PO 0.912 (-0.286, 25 teams); PNR -0.173; PULL_UP +0.301; others within -0.07.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: DRIVE playoff PPP 0.286 below RS across 25 teams; top-10 teams all -0.30 to -0.43.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 25 teams, min 30 poss per cell; no CIs\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Team-level (team, PT, context) cells, min 30 poss, up to 25 teams.\n- observed_verdict: supported\n- observed_failure_type: D_positive\n- observed_notes: Motivated the playoff DRIVE exclusion and a proposed playoff DSI offset."}, {"id": "FAM:SF-PAP-016", "score": 0.102, "document": "# FAM:SF-PAP-016 | Study family SF-PAP-016: Portability feasibility gate\n- observed_research_question: Portability feasibility gate\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Enough movers with decoys exist and displacement signature is not collinear with play-type profile.\n- observed_result: Prereg: 296 movers, decoy frac 1.00, vacuity rho=0.048; final output: 294 movers, rho=0.007\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: gate passed\n- observed_sample_and_power: 296/294 movers\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF19\n- observed_method: Mover signature cache; G1 >=25 movers, G2 >=80% with >=3 decoys, G3 |rho|<0.90.\n- observed_verdict: supported\n- observed_failure_type: D_positive\n- observed_notes: Mover count and vacuity rho changed between prereg record and final output.\n- auto_confidence: high (1.0)\n- auto_addresses_question: RQC:RQC-051\n- auto_uses_method: METH:correlation"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-PAP-009", "score": 0.094, "document": "# FAM:SF-PAP-009 | Study family SF-PAP-009: Coverage feasibility gate\n- observed_research_question: Coverage feasibility gate\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Lineup coverage (>=1 organizer, shaper, terminal) varies within team, is separable from talent/counts, and talent control behaves.\n- observed_result: G1 72 team-seasons with >=200 poss in both; G2 |rho(COVERED,TALENT)|=0.042, aux R2=0.203; G3 rho(TALENT,PPP)=+0.027\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: gate passed\n- observed_sample_and_power: 90 team-seasons\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF29\n- observed_method: 420,993 possessions, 90 team-seasons; 3 gate criteria, beta not computed.\n- observed_verdict: supported\n- observed_failure_type: D_positive\n- observed_notes: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_confidence: high (1.0)\n- auto_addresses_question: RQC:RQC-050\n- auto_uses_method: METH:correlation\n- observed_member_records: PAP-009"}, {"id": "FAM:SF29", "score": 0.08, "document": "# FAM:SF29 | Study family SF29: Coverage > accumulation confirmatory (T_cov)\n- observed_research_question: Coverage > accumulation confirmatory (T_cov)\n- auto_outcome_status: rejected\n- observed_hypothesis: Lineups covering all three core roles score more per possession net of role counts and talent.\n- observed_result: [APPM-042] Gate PASS (COVERED 30.0%; 72 team-seasons both strata; |Spearman(COVERED,TALENT)|=0.042; R2(COVERED~counts)=0.203; Spearman(TALENT,PPP)=+0.027). M1 COVERED b=+0.0067 (+0.67 pts/100), t=1.35, p=0.176, team-seas [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- observed_result: [PAP-010] Final: beta=+0.42 pts/100, t=0.53, p=0.595, CI[-1.15,+1.90]; MDE80=2.19 pts/100; n_ORGANIZER +2.35 (t=4.62). Prereg-recorded run (2026-07-13): +0.67 pts/100, t=1.35, p=0.176, CI[-0.28,+1.65]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_power_large_MDE\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_verdict: [APPM-042] null"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
